@startuml
title Set exchange rates (administrator)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Bank administrator" as admin
participant "Admin Web App\n(React SPA)" as spa
participant "Core Banking API\n(FastAPI)" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

admin -> spa : Opens Exchange rates and enters: base currency, target currency, rate
spa -> spa : Validates the form (rate > 0, base != target, max 6 decimal places)
spa -> api : POST /admin/exchange-rates\n{baseCurrency, targetCurrency, rate}
api -> api : Authenticates the token (signature, expiry) and reads user id

alt invalid or missing token
    api --> spa : 401 Unauthorized
    spa --> admin : Redirects to login
else token valid
    api -> db : SELECT role, status FROM users WHERE id = :user_id
    db --> api : role, status
    alt status <> 'ACTIVE' or role <> 'ADMIN'
        api --> spa : 403 Forbidden
        spa --> admin : Shows "access denied"
    else active ADMIN
        api -> api : Normalizes codes to upper case and validates the payload\n(codes match ^[A-Z]{3}$, base != target, 0 < rate < 10^6, max 6 decimal places)
        alt invalid payload
            api --> spa : 422 Unprocessable Entity (validation errors)
            spa --> admin : Shows validation errors
        else payload valid
            api -> db : SELECT code FROM currencies\nWHERE code IN (:base, :target)
            db --> api : existing currency codes
            alt unknown currency
                api --> spa : 422 Unprocessable Entity (unknown currency)
                spa --> admin : Shows error message
            else currencies exist
                api -> api : inverse rate = ROUND(1 / rate, 6)
                api -> db : BEGIN;\nINSERT INTO exchange_rates (base_currency, target_currency, rate, rate_timestamp)\nVALUES (:base, :target, :rate, :now_utc),\n       (:target, :base, :inverse_rate, :now_utc)\nRETURNING id;\nCOMMIT
                db --> api : ids of both rows
                api -> api : Logs the change (admin user id, pair, rate) to the application audit log
                api --> spa : 201 Created {id, baseCurrency, targetCurrency, rate, inverseRate, rateTimestamp}
                spa --> admin : Shows confirmation and the updated rates list
            end
        end
    end
end

note over api, db
Rates are never updated: each change inserts new rows (both directions),
the current rate of a pair is its newest row
(ORDER BY rate_timestamp DESC, id DESC LIMIT 1). Old rows keep the history.
Transfers already in progress keep the rate they read before the change.
end note
@enduml
